it's been more than 10 years since the  original Avatar dominated the box office  with its amazing visuals and immersive  3D during the long wait for part two the  filmmakers came up with and then set  aside a sequel you'll never get to see  at least not in theaters  director James Cameron is the force  behind many iconic films from Terminator  to Titanic but the most successful is  undeniably Avatar which premiered in  2009 and swiftly became the biggest  movie ever made you know the story Jake  Sully is a former Marine who becomes  enamored with the world of Pandora in  the guise of an avatar who looks like  them he grows close with the natives the  navi and elects to help them in their  fight to defend their home from  exploitation it took years for Avatar to  become a reality and once it did it  became nothing short of a global  phenomenon it grossed billions of  dollars at the global box office and the  vast majority of audiences and critics  seemed to adore it despite that  unprecedented success it's taken more  than 10 years for the sequel Avatar the  way of water to become a reality the  long-awaited follow-up will hit theaters  on December 16 2022 intending to pave  the way for three more sequels that will  arrive in the years to come time will  tell if these films stay on track but  it's clear that James Cameron is  treating this franchise meticulously  even scrapping one sequel entirely after  he had completed the script as he  recently revealed the original concept  for Avatar 2 looked quite different from  what the way of water turned out to be  ahead of the theatrical arrival of  Avatar the way of water James Cameron  spoke to Total film about the Avatar  world and all of the work that has gone  into it along the way he touched on his  initial idea for a sequel to the 2009  sensation titled avatar The High Ground  Cameron recalled I was working with a  team of writers we had a lot of ideas we  kept trying to Corral it into a box and  it never quite fit so at a certain point  I said I'll just finish it and see if  it's a movie when it was all said and  done Cameron said the 130 page script  was excellent and told a compelling  story at the same time Cameron admits  that The High Ground script wasn't quite  up to par for reasons he couldn't quite  put his finger on he told the  publication it was missing one of those  critical elements about sequels which is  that it didn't go enough into the  unexpected the story also didn't play by  what Cameron refers to as Avatar rules  meaning it didn't quite tap into the  spiritual nature of the previous film  with that Cameron and his crew went back  to the drawing board board they  eventually landed on the concept that  became the way of water and the rest is  history let's get it done so far all we  know about Avatar The High Ground is  what James Cameron has divulged but he's  about to reveal a whole lot more as he  described to Total film there's some  great stuff in it I mean you've got the  navi fighting with bows and arrows and  zero g I want to see that movie while  you won't quite see it as a movie you  will get to see the ideas in action as  Cameron revealed we're turning it into a  dark horse graphic novel you'll be able  to see that interim battle that took  place between Movie 1 and movie 2. The  Graphic novel will arrive on December  6th 2022 just 10 days before the way of  water Premiere fans of the franchise  won't want to miss out not if they want  the full story anyway from the new film  and theaters to this scrapped sequel  seeing the light of day not to mention  the three movies still to come if the  way of water performs well it's a great  time to be an avatar fan for the first  time in quite a while  [Music]
 

